{
  "$comment": "Bravo buttons: the trim wheel, autopilot panel, gear lever and the seven switches. Two halves. 'controls' is the PHYSICAL map - which button number each control is - and it is MEASURED by Probe-HoneycombDevices.ps1 -Capture, never typed in: 'prober' is the number the prober prints (Windows' 1-based count), 'fsuipc' is FSUIPC's number for the same button (prober - 1, and above 31 FSUIPC reports from 132), and 'verified' is true only after the capture has seen it pressed. Set-BravoButtons.ps1 refuses to write any control that is not verified. 'map' is the CHOICE of what each control does in the sim - control numbers from the Controls List that ships with FSUIPC - and it is a decision to review, not a measurement. Switches send explicit ON on press and OFF on release rather than a toggle, so the switch position and the sim always agree. The INCR/DECR rotary depends on the mode selector: FSUIPC compound conditions, one line per mode.",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "device": { "name": "Bravo Throttle Quadrant", "vid": "294B", "pid": "1901" },
  "numbering": "fsuipc = prober - 1; if that is above 31, add 100 (FSUIPC User Guide: buttons > 31 are numbered from 132). Measured on Mark's Bravo: prober 33 = FSUIPC 132.",

